            ],
            "ref": "refs/changes/73/89173/1",
            "uploader": {
                "name": "Vinoth Kumar Shanmugavel",
                "email": "vinothkumars@ami.com",
                "username": "VinothKumar-AMI"
            },
            "createdOn": 1775974978,
            "author": {
                "name": "Vinoth Kumar Shanmugavel",
                "email": "vinothkumars@ami.com",
                "username": "VinothKumar-AMI"
            },
            "kind": "REWORK",
            "comments": [
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 37,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Gunnar Mills",
                        "email": "gunnar@gmills.xyz",
                        "username": "gtmills"
                    },
                    "message": "Thanks for this commit! Can you use your full name here? Best also to use in Gerrit if possible. \n\"All commit messages must include a \"Signed-off-by\" line, which indicates that you the contributor have agreed to the Developer Certificate of Origin (see below). This line must include the full name you commonly use, often a given name and a family name or surname. (ok: Sam Samuelsson, Robert A. Heinlein; not ok: xXthorXx, Sam, RAH)\"\n\nhttps://github.com/openbmc/docs/blob/c79ac7da8d90bba82508c99e16a09ec5685f0c25/CONTRIBUTING.md?plain=1#L251"
                },
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 37,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Patrick Williams",
                        "email": "patrick@stwcx.xyz",
                        "username": "williamspatrick"
                    },
                    "message": "This would have also been flagged by Jenkins but they don't seem to be in a CLA."
                },
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 37,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Vinoth Kumar Shanmugavel",
                        "email": "vinothkumars@ami.com",
                        "username": "VinothKumar-AMI"
                    },
                    "message": "Thanks for the reminder! I\u2019ve updated my commit to use my full name in the Signed-off-by line and in my Gerrit profile.\nIf there are any further issues with the DCO or CLA, please let me know."
                },
                {
                    "file": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
                    "line": 0,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Vinoth Kumar Shanmugavel",
                        "email": "vinothkumars@ami.com",
                        "username": "VinothKumar-AMI"
                    },
                    "message": "There is already dynamic handling for JSON schemas in bmcweb, implemented in redfish_v1.hpp. Specifically, the following routes are registered (see https://github.com/openbmc/bmcweb/blob/master/redfish-core/lib/redfish_v1.hpp#L251-L258). These routes already provide dynamic serving of JSON schema files, so there is no need to add new dynamic handling for JSON schemas in this commit, it's already present and working as intended."
                },
                {
                    "file": "include/authentication.hpp",
                    "line": 230,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Gunnar Mills",
                        "email": "gunnar@gmills.xyz",
                        "username": "gtmills"
                    },
                    "message": "Have to solve Ed's comment below first but do you need /redfish/v1/schema here? \n\nI don't think \nurl.starts_with(\"/redfish/v1/schema/\") returns true when /redfish/v1/schema"
                },
                {
                    "file": "include/authentication.hpp",
                    "line": 230,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Vinoth Kumar Shanmugavel",
                        "email": "vinothkumars@ami.com",
                        "username": "VinothKumar-AMI"
                    },
                    "message": "The current implementation also did not support a schema collection endpoint. It only registered individual schema file routes.\nMy dynamic implementation maintains the same behavior. I only handle individual schema file requests via /redfish/v1/schema/<str>/, not a collection endpoint.\nThe allowlist check starts_with(\"/redfish/v1/schema/\") is intentional and correct:\n/redfish/v1/schema \u2192 does not match (no trailing slash, not allowed)\n/redfish/v1/schema/AccountService.xml \u2192 matches and proceeds to validation\nSo the schema collection endpoint is not on the allowlist and remains inaccessible, which is consistent with the existing behavior."
                },
                {
                    "file": "include/authentication.hpp",
                    "line": 238,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ed Tanous",
                        "email": "ed@tanous.net",
                        "username": "edtanous"
                    },
                    "message": "Generally we don't allow starts_with type comparisons.  This is a security boundary, so we need to be somewhat specific, that's why the old check used a specific list of routes.  If someone registered /redfish/v1/schema/sensitive_data, this would allow them through.\n\nlet me think on this a bit on how to solve this, as your use case makes sense, but this check was very intentionally not a starts_with type request."
                },
                {
                    "file": "include/authentication.hpp",
                    "line": 238,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Vinoth Kumar Shanmugavel",
                        "email": "vinothkumars@ami.com",
                        "username": "VinothKumar-AMI"
                    },
                    "message": "Thank you for the feedback. I understand the security concern with using starts_with here. My intent was to allow only schema XML files to be accessed without authentication, but I agree that a more precise check is safer. I've updated the check to be more specific. \nThis approach:\nOnly allows URLs matching the pattern - /redfish/v1/schema/<filename>.xml\nEnsures the filename is not empty - (prevents /redfish/v1/schema/.xml)\nDisallows subdirectories - (prevents /redfish/v1/schema/subdir/file.xml)\nThis maintains the security boundary while allowing the legitimate use case of serving XML schema files dynamically. Please let me know if you'd like any further refinements."
                },
                {
                    "file": "include/webassets.hpp",
                    "line": 263,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Patrick Williams",
                        "email": "patrick@stwcx.xyz",
                        "username": "williamspatrick"
                    },
                    "message": "Why is there special handling here for JsonSchema but no where else in the commit?  Do you forget to add support for JsonSchema?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "include/webassets.hpp",
                    "line": 263,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Vinoth Kumar Shanmugavel",
                        "email": "vinothkumars@ami.com",
                        "username": "VinothKumar-AMI"
                    },
                    "message": "There is already dynamic handling for JSON schemas in bmcweb, implemented in redfish_v1.hpp. Specifically, the following routes are registered (see https://github.com/openbmc/bmcweb/blob/master/redfish-core/lib/redfish_v1.hpp#L251-L258). These routes already provide dynamic serving of JSON schema files, so there is no need to add new dynamic handling for JSON schemas in this commit, it's already present and working as intended."
                },
                {
                    "file": "include/webassets.hpp",
                    "line": 263,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ed Tanous",
                        "email": "ed@tanous.net",
                        "username": "edtanous"
                    },
                    "message": "Please just move where these files are installed.  If we're not going to use the static file hosting, don't put them in the static file hosting folder, and they won't be scanned."
                },
                {
                    "file": "include/webassets.hpp",
                    "line": 263,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ed Tanous",
                        "email": "ed@tanous.net",
                        "username": "edtanous"
                    },
                    "message": "I'd also add that I see this as one of the main benefits of this patch: You can disable static hosting entirely and still host a correct Redfish tree.  That would be very valuable for people that ship without the webui enabled."
                },
                {
                    "file": "include/webassets.hpp",
                    "line": 263,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Vinoth Kumar Shanmugavel",
                        "email": "vinothkumars@ami.com",
                        "username": "VinothKumar-AMI"
                    },
                    "message": "Thank you, Ed. That makes sense. Do you have a recommended directory or location where the schema files should be installed now that they\u2019re not served statically?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "include/webassets.hpp",
                    "line": 263,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ed Tanous",
                        "email": "ed@tanous.net",
                        "username": "edtanous"
                    },
                    "message": "/usr/share/redfish-schema-pack is where the existing recipes install it I believe.  No strong opinion."
                },
                {
                    "file": "redfish-core/lib/metadata.hpp",
                    "line": 133,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ed Tanous",
                        "email": "ed@tanous.net",
                        "username": "edtanous"
                    },
                    "message": "This is now unauthenticated code that could (potentially) let an attacker read any file.  Schema needs to be checked against every known pattern we see in schemas (alphanum + version + xml) before we attempt to open the filesystem, otherwise you can escape out and read any file.  As written, i'm pretty sure this is a CVE.  FWIW, that CVE is why we initially used a scanned list built at startup, as it's easy to verify the correctness of."
                },
                {
                    "file": "redfish-core/lib/metadata.hpp",
                    "line": 133,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Gunnar Mills",
                        "email": "gunnar@gmills.xyz",
                        "username": "gtmills"
                    },
                    "message": "+1\n\nfilePath = \"/usr/share/www/redfish/v1/schema/../../../../../<dir>/<file>\"\nPasses"
                },
                {
                    "file": "redfish-core/lib/metadata.hpp",
                    "line": 133,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Vinoth Kumar Shanmugavel",
                        "email": "vinothkumars@ami.com",
                        "username": "VinothKumar-AMI"
                    },
                    "message": "Thank you for pointing out the CVE risk. I\u2019ve added strict validation to only allow safe .xml filenames and block any path traversal before accessing the filesystem. This should fully address the vulnerability. Please let me know if you see any other concerns."
                },
                {
                    "file": "redfish-core/lib/metadata.hpp",
                    "line": 133,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ed Tanous",
                        "email": "ed@tanous.net",
                        "username": "edtanous"
                    },
                    "message": "> This should fully address the vulnerability\n\nCurrent patch does not appear to implement what I asked for."
